## 5. Remaining screens

- `lib/hatchway/pages/empty_air_page.dart` → `Insight.screen('offline');`
  + `Insight.event('offline_retry');` in the Retry handler.
- White-part screens (`lib/screens/*`) → `Insight.screen('menu' | 'levels'
  | 'game');` in `initState` (convert `StatelessWidget` → `StatefulWidget`
  if needed; do not spam from `build`).

---

## 6. The funnel you get in the dashboard

```
route_web → web_open → web_offer_reached ─┐ (or web_offer_unreachable + reason)
                                          ├→ web_register_page/click → web_register_submit
                                          ├→ web_login_page/click    → web_login_submit
                                          └→ web_cashier_page        → web_deposit_click
```
Slice by tags: `aid`, `run_mode`, `last_screen`, `notif_permission`,
`offer_reached`, `web_error_reason`, `reached_register/login/cashier`.

## 7. Hard rules
- ❌ Never call the Clarity SDK directly — always through `Insight`
  (guarded). A Clarity failure must never break the gray flow.
- ❌ Never reuse a Clarity `projectId` across projects (`[FINGERPRINT]`).
- ❌ Never ship the same JS-channel name / sentinel across apps
  (`[FINGERPRINT]`) — see `gray_part_mixing_review.mdc`.
- ✅ Keep event names STABLE and few; put high-cardinality values (urls,
  hosts, labels, error text) in TAGS, not event names.
- ✅ `identify()` only after `af_id` is known (post `buildPayload`).
- ✅ The JS probe must stay idempotent (`window.__lavaInsight` guard).
